.TH ATPROBE 1
.SH NAME
atprobe \- exercise directory-fd filesystem syscalls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atprobe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atprobe
is a regression probe for SmallOS directory-fd and POSIX-style
.BR *at ()
filesystem behavior. It verifies relative operations against directory file
descriptors, absolute-path override, non-directory base failures, hard links,
symbolic links, no-follow stat and timestamp updates, and
.BR unlinkat ()
directory removal.
.PP
The probe is installed under
.I /usr/libexec/tests
and is normally run by the shell selftest and host ELF regression harness.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 when every check passes, or 1 after printing failed check names.
